On a finite probability space with $cal(F) = cal(P)(Omega)$ and $PP(A) = abs(A) \/ abs(Omega)$, multiplying by $abs(Omega)$ turns the formula into
$
  abs(union.big_(i=1)^n A_i) = sum_(k=1)^n (-1)^(k+1) (sum_(1 <= i_1 < ... < i_k <= n) abs(A_(i_1) inter ... inter A_(i_k))),
$
the inclusion-exclusion principle of combinatorics.
